---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Internal Comms 2026: From Newsletter Writer to Context Architect | Word And Mouth">
  <main class="solved-page">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-content">
        <span class="category-tag">THE GREENHOUSE</span>
        <h1>Internal Comms 2026</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">When Your Colleagues Include Autonomous Agents</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Problem Everyone Saw -->
    <section class="story-section problem-visible">
      <div class="section-marker">01</div>
      <h2>The Problem Everyone Saw</h2>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p class="lead">"AI will replace the company newsletter."</p>
        <p>
          Every comms professional has heard it. The assumption that generative AI would simply 
          automate content creation—churning out emails, intranet articles, and town hall summaries 
          faster than any human team.
        </p>
        <p>
          Leadership imagined efficiency gains. Vendors promised "AI-powered internal comms platforms." 
          The industry responded with predictable anxiety about job security.
        </p>
        <div class="insight-card">
          <span class="icon">📧</span>
          <p>The conversation centred on <strong>content production</strong>—who writes the emails, 
          who drafts the policies, who summarises the all-hands.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Problem That Was Actually There -->
    <section class="story-section problem-hidden">
      <div class="section-marker">02</div>
      <h2>The Problem That Was Actually There</h2>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p class="lead">The real crisis isn't content. It's context.</p>
        <p>
          By 2026, the "workforce" has bifurcated into carbon-based and silicon-based employees. 
          Autonomous agents don't just wait for instructions—they observe, plan, execute, and 
          collaborate. They access data through Model Context Protocols (MCP), chain complex 
          workflows, and make decisions that impact physical and financial reality.
        </p>
        
        <div class="framework-box">
          <h3>The Context Crisis</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Agents need structured knowledge</strong> — not prose, not ambiguity, not "read between the lines"</li>
            <li><strong>Humans need psychological safety</strong> — clarity on what's automated, what's human, what's trustworthy</li>
            <li><strong>Both need consistency</strong> — if the CEO says one thing and the policy says another, agents crash or hallucinate</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p>
          The Internal Communications professional must now act as the architect of understanding 
          across a hybrid divide—ensuring that the "culture-energy chasm" doesn't swallow the 
          human innovation that remains the company's core differentiator.
        </p>

        <div class="impact-stat">
          <span class="stat-number">2,000+</span>
          <span class="stat-label">"Death by AI" legal claims predicted by Gartner for 2026—corporate fatalities 
          driven by black-box systems misfiring</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Unexpected Solution -->
    <section class="story-section solution">
      <div class="section-marker">03</div>
      <h2>The Unexpected Solution</h2>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p class="lead">The IC Manager becomes the Chief Context Officer.</p>
        
        <div class="solution-grid">
          <div class="solution-card">
            <h4>Context Architecture</h4>
            <p>Structure information so it's intelligible to both humans and agents. 
            Tag, categorise, and link within enterprise knowledge graphs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="solution-card">
            <h4>Brand Twin Governance</h4>
            <p>Curate the personality of your company's AI representatives. 
            Oversee RLHF loops that train agent responses to align with culture.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="solution-card">
            <h4>HITL Protocols</h4>
            <p>Design escalation matrices. Define when humans must intervene. 
            Ensure employees know when they're talking to a machine.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="solution-card">
            <h4>Sentiment Mission Control</h4>
            <p>Real-time dashboards aggregating tone from Slack, agent queries, 
            and wellness data. Predict crises before they become turnover.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="evolution-table">
          <h3>The IC Evolution</h3>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Dimension</th>
                <th>Traditional IC (2020s)</th>
                <th>Agentic IC (2026)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Primary Output</td>
                <td>Content (Emails, Articles)</td>
                <td>Context (Knowledge Graphs, Agent Personas)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Audience</td>
                <td>Human Employees</td>
                <td>Humans & Autonomous Agents</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Key Metric</td>
                <td>Engagement (Open Rates)</td>
                <td>Alignment (Sentiment, Adoption)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Crisis Role</td>
                <td>Drafting Statements</td>
                <td>Managing Agent Governance</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What You Can Steal -->
    <section class="story-section steal">
      <div class="section-marker">04</div>
      <h2>What You Can Steal</h2>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p class="lead">Four literacies every organisation needs now.</p>
        
        <div class="steal-grid">
          <div class="steal-item">
            <span class="steal-number">01</span>
            <h4>Agentic Orchestration</h4>
            <p>Teach your people to decompose complex objectives into discrete tasks 
            assignable to specific agents. Create "Agent Persona cards" describing 
            what each agent is good and bad at.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="steal-item">
            <span class="steal-number">02</span>
            <h4>Context Engineering</h4>
            <p>Train structured communication—writing with precision, no ambiguity, 
            logical flow. Create templates that force necessary context fields 
            before agents accept tasks.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="steal-item">
            <span class="steal-number">03</span>
            <h4>Algorithmic Skepticism</h4>
            <p>Build verification reflexes. Never trust agent outputs without 
            checking sources. Develop "Explainable AI" communication that shows 
            the why behind decisions.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="steal-item">
            <span class="steal-number">04</span>
            <h4>Emotional Resilience</h4>
            <p>Address the psychological impact head-on. The fear isn't job loss—it's 
            loss of voice and autonomy. Build high-empathy, narrative-rich 
            communication layers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="greenhouse-cta">
          <h3>🌱 The Greenhouse Connection</h3>
          <p>
            Internal Communications is a core capability of The Greenhouse—our embedded 
            transformation programme. We help organisations build the infrastructure 
            for human-AI collaboration before the crisis arrives.
          </p>
          <a href="/services/the-greenhouse" class="cta-button">Explore The Greenhouse →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="final-cta">
      <h2>Ready to Future-Proof Your Internal Comms?</h2>
      <p>The transition is happening. The question is whether you're architecting it or reacting to it.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="primary-cta">Start the Conversation</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .solved-page {
    --gold: #D4AF37;
    --dark: #0a0a0a;
    --light: #f5f5f5;
    color: var(--light);
    background: var(--dark);
  }

  /* Hero */
  .hero {
    min-height: 60vh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #0a0a0a 100%);
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
  }

  .category-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.2);
    border: 1px solid var(--gold);
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff 0%, var(--gold) 100%);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    opacity: 0.8;
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* Story Sections */
  .story-section {
    padding: 6rem 2rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    position: relative;
  }

  .section-marker {
    position: absolute;
    top: 4rem;
    left: -2rem;
    font-size: 4rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    opacity: 0.1;
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .story-section h2 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .content-block p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  /* Insight Card */
  .insight-card {
    background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.1);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .insight-card .icon {
    font-size: 2rem;
  }

  .insight-card p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Framework Box */
  .framework-box {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    padding: 2rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .framework-box h3 {
    color: var(--gold);
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .framework-box ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .framework-box li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Impact Stat */
  .impact-stat {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.2) 0%, rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.05) 100%);
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .stat-number {
    display: block;
    font-size: 3.5rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .stat-label {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  /* Solution Grid */
  .solution-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .solution-card {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .solution-card:hover {
    background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.1);
    border-color: var(--gold);
  }

  .solution-card h4 {
    color: var(--gold);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .solution-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  /* Evolution Table */
  .evolution-table {
    margin: 3rem 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .evolution-table h3 {
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .evolution-table table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .evolution-table th,
  .evolution-table td {
    padding: 1rem;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  }

  .evolution-table th {
    background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.2);
    color: var(--gold);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .evolution-table tr:hover td {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }

  /* Steal Grid */
  .steal-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .steal-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .steal-number {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--gold);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .steal-item h4 {
    color: #fff;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .steal-item p {
    margin: 0;
    opacity: 0.85;
    grid-column: 2;
  }

  /* Greenhouse CTA */
  .greenhouse-cta {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(34, 139, 34, 0.2) 0%, rgba(34, 139, 34, 0.05) 100%);
    border: 1px solid rgba(34, 139, 34, 0.3);
    padding: 2rem;
    margin: 3rem 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .greenhouse-cta h3 {
    color: #90EE90;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .greenhouse-cta p {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .cta-button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.75rem 2rem;
    background: rgba(34, 139, 34, 0.3);
    border: 1px solid #90EE90;
    color: #90EE90;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .cta-button:hover {
    background: #90EE90;
    color: #0a0a0a;
  }

  /* Final CTA */
  .final-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 6rem 2rem;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.1) 0%, transparent 100%);
  }

  .final-cta h2 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .final-cta p {
    opacity: 0.8;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .primary-cta {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 1rem 3rem;
    background: var(--gold);
    color: var(--dark);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .primary-cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .section-marker {
      position: static;
      font-size: 2rem;
      opacity: 0.3;
    }
    
    .steal-item {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    
    .steal-number {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
    
    .steal-item p {
      grid-column: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
